{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VeM3vqYiw41v5HAnGV7Zp6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 原始 framing 的两个支柱均不成立：(1) 'episode-level 就够了' 被 GAE 大幅超越反驳（finer\n2\t  credit 确实必要），(2) 'catastrophic failure at small h' 被不一致的 h-sweep 削弱（部分 seed h=5\n3\t  也能学到 15-20%）。Contrarian positioning 崩塌。需要完全 reframe 为 empirical taxonomy 或 sufficient\n4\t  conditions 研究。Selective verification 因 base agent 太弱（<30%）完全不可行。\n5\timagined_experiments:\n6\t- name: Context window h-sweep ablation (3 seeds each)\n7\t  plan_id: plan_002\n8\t  description: Sweep h={2, 5, 10, 20, full}, 15 steps, 3 seeds each. 测试 credit assignment\n9\t    cliff 是否 robust。\n10\t  expected_results:\n11\t    h2_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.0\n12\t    h2_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.031\n13\t    h2_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.0\n14\t    h5_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.156\n15\t    h5_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.0\n16\t    h5_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.188\n17\t    h10_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.094\n18\t    h10_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.219\n19\t    h10_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.125\n20\t    h20_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.188\n21\t    h20_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.25\n22\t    h20_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.156\n23\t    full_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.25\n24\t    full_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.281\n25\t    full_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.219\n26\t    collapse_rate_h2: 0.67\n27\t    collapse_rate_h5: 0.33\n28\t    collapse_rate_h10: 0.0\n29\t    cliff_threshold_range: 3-8 (seed-dependent)\n30\t  result_rationale: Worst 档下 h-sweep cliff 不一致。h=2 多数 seed 崩溃但非全部（seed2 靠运气学到少量 pattern）。h=5\n31\t    更关键：seed1/3 没有崩溃且学到 15-19%，只有 seed2 崩溃。这直接削弱 'catastrophic failure below threshold'\n32\t    narrative——cliff 位置是 stochastic 的，不是 deterministic 的。h=10/20/full 之间差异不大（均在 10-25%\n33\t    区间），说明即使给了足够 context，episode-level 本身也有天花板。Monotonic degradation 假设不成立：h=5 的某些\n34\t    seed 可以接近 h=full。\n35\t  tables:\n36\t  - name: 'Table 1: h-sweep results (mean ± std across 3 seeds)'\n37\t    columns:\n38\t    - h\n39\t    - val_success_mean\n40\t    - val_success_std\n41\t    - collapse_rate\n42\t    - convergence_step\n43\t    rows:\n44\t    - - 2\n45\t      - 1.0%\n46\t      - 1.8%\n47\t      - 67%\n48\t      - 3-4\n49\t    - - 5\n50\t      - 11.5%\n51\t      - 10.4%\n52\t      - 33%\n53\t      - 4-6\n54\t    - - 10\n55\t      - 14.6%\n56\t      - 6.3%\n57\t      - 0%\n58\t      - N/A\n59\t    - - 20\n60\t      - 19.8%\n61\t      - 4.8%\n62\t      - 0%\n63\t      - N/A\n64\t    - - full\n65\t      - 25.0%\n66\t      - 3.1%\n67\t      - 0%\n68\t      - N/A\n69\t  figures_description:\n70\t  - 'Fig: h-value vs val_success with per-seed lines. 无 clean cliff——h=5 区间有巨大 variance\n71\t    band（0-19%），与 h=10 overlap。Error bars 在 h=5 处最宽。'\n72\t  analysis: Cliff 不 robust。h=5 std=10.4pp 意味着 cliff 位置是 random variable 而非 structural\n73\t    property。无法 claim 'h<X catastrophically fails' 因为 X 取决于 seed。这削弱了 paper 的核心 figure\n74\t    说服力——reviewer 会问 'with more seeds would the cliff disappear entirely?'\n75\t- name: Multi-seed replication (5 seeds total)\n76\t  plan_id: plan_003\n77\t  description: 4 additional seeds for exp029 episode-level config, report mean ± std。\n78\t  expected_results:\n79\t    seed1_val_success_step15: 0.281\n80\t    seed2_val_success_step15: 0.188\n81\t    seed3_val_success_step15: 0.313\n82\t    seed4_val_success_step15: 0.156\n83\t    seed5_val_success_step15: 0.25\n84\t    mean_val_success: 0.238\n85\t    std_val_success: 0.062\n86\t    max_val_success_any_seed: 0.313\n87\t    min_val_success_any_seed: 0.156\n88\t    seeds_above_30pct: 1\n89\t    seeds_below_20pct: 1\n90\t    convergence_step_range: 10-15 (all plateau)\n91\t    step50_mean_val_success: 0.26\n92\t    step50_std: 0.071\n93\t  result_rationale: Worst 档要求 multi_seed_std > 8pp。5 seeds 中 std=6.2pp（接近但略低于阈值），但如果看\n94\t    step 50（训练更久），seed 4 可能进一步恶化（plateau 后缓慢下降到 12-15%），使得 late-stage std 达到 8-10pp。关键问题：seed\n95\t    4 只有 15.6%，与 step-independent h=10 的 best seed（21.9%）重叠——episode-level 的 advantage\n96\t    over step-independent 在 per-seed 层面不 universal。reproducibility 不够 strong（CI 太宽），reviewer\n97\t    会 flag 'your method might just be getting lucky on some seeds'。\n98\t  tables:\n99\t  - name: 'Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level GRPO results'\n100\t    columns:\n101\t    - seed\n102\t    - step5_val\n103\t    - step10_val\n104\t    - step15_val\n105\t    - step50_val\n106\t    - plateau_onset\n107\t    rows:\n108\t    - - 1\n109\t      - 25.0%\n110\t      - 25.0%\n111\t      - 28.1%\n112\t      - 28.1%\n113\t      - step 10\n114\t    - - 2\n115\t      - 18.8%\n116\t      - 18.8%\n117\t      - 18.8%\n118\t      - 21.9%\n119\t      - step 5\n120\t    - - 3\n121\t      - 25.0%\n122\t      - 31.3%\n123\t      - 31.3%\n124\t      - 31.3%\n125\t      - step 10\n126\t    - - 4\n127\t      - 12.5%\n128\t      - 15.6%\n129\t      - 15.6%\n130\t      - 15.6%\n131\t      - step 5\n132\t    - - 5\n133\t      - 18.8%\n134\t      - 25.0%\n135\t      - 25.0%\n136\t      - 28.1%\n137\t      - step 10\n138\t  figures_description:\n139\t  - 'Fig: Training curves (5 seeds) with shaded std band. Band 宽度在 step 5 后稳定但 wide（±6pp），所有\n140\t    seed 在 step 10-15 plateau，无 seed 突破 32%。'\n141\t  analysis: Mean 23.8% ± 6.2pp。95% CI = [11.3%, 36.3%]。这个 CI 与 step-independent h=10\n142\t    mean（14.6%）有 overlap，削弱 episode-level 的统计 significance。更致命的是 plateau 现象——所有 seed\n143\t    在 step 10-15 停滞，额外训练 35 步几乎无改善，说明 episode-level GRPO 本身有信息瓶颈（无 per-token credit）。\n144\t- name: GAE baseline comparison\n145\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n146\t  description: GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps\n147\t    × 3 seeds。\n148\t  expected_results:\n149\t    gae_095_mean_val_success_step15: 0.438\n150\t    gae_095_std: 0.047\n151\t    gae_100_mean_val_success_step15: 0.375\n152\t    gae_100_std: 0.055\n153\t    episode_grpo_mean_val_success_step15: 0.238\n154\t    gae_095_vs_episode_delta_pp: 20.0\n155\t    gae_100_vs_episode_delta_pp: 13.7\n156\t    gae_095_action_is_valid: 0.78\n157\t    gae_095_convergence_step: 12\n158\t    gae_still_improving_at_step15: true\n159\t  result_rationale: Worst 档核心假设：GAE >> episode-level GRPO（delta > 15pp）。GAE(0.95)\n160\t    有 value function 做 per-token credit assignment，能区分 trajectory 中好/坏 action 并精确更新。Episode-level\n161\t    GRPO 所有 token 共享一个 advantage（相当于 REINFORCE），缺乏 temporal difference 信息。20pp gap\n162\t    证明 per-token credit 是关键——episode-level 'just knowing the outcome' 不够，你需要知道 which\n163\t    tokens contributed。这直接反驳 paper 的 contrarian claim 'coarser is better'。GAE(1.0,1.0)\n164\t    稍弱因为 high variance（相当于 Monte Carlo），但仍优于 GRPO 因为 critic 提供 baseline。\n165\t  tables:\n166\t  - name: 'Table 3: GAE vs Episode-level GRPO'\n167\t    columns:\n168\t    - method\n169\t    - val_success_mean\n170\t    - std\n171\t    - delta_vs_episode_grpo\n172\t    - action_is_valid\n173\t    - still_improving\n174\t    rows:\n175\t    - - Episode GRPO\n176\t      - 23.8%\n177\t      - 6.2pp\n178\t      - —\n179\t      - 55%\n180\t      - No (plateau)\n181\t    - - GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0)\n182\t      - 37.5%\n183\t      - 5.5pp\n184\t      - +13.7pp\n185\t      - 72%\n186\t      - Marginal\n187\t    - - GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0)\n188\t      - 43.8%\n189\t      - 4.7pp\n190\t      - +20.0pp\n191\t      - 78%\n192\t      - 'Yes'\n193\t  figures_description:\n194\t  - 'Fig: Learning curves — GAE(0.95) clearly dominates from step 5 onward, with episode\n195\t    GRPO plateauing while GAE continues climbing. The gap widens over training.'\n196\t  analysis: GAE 大幅超越 episode-level GRPO 证明 per-token temporal difference credit 是关键。Episode-level\n197\t    的 'advantage sign is correct' 不够——你还需要 magnitude differentiation across tokens。这反驳了\n198\t    contrarian positioning：社区追求 finer credit 是对的。Episode-level 只是 '方向不错但信息太粗' 的 solution。Paper\n199\t    的核心 contribution（'coarser suffices'）被实验数据否定。\n200\t- name: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus (plateau-breaker)\n201\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n202\t  description: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 测试能否打破 plateau 且不 game。\n203\t  expected_results:\n204\t    val_success_step15: 0.25\n205\t    val_action_is_valid_step15: 0.72\n206\t    val_action_is_valid_step30: 0.85\n207\t    success_plateau_broken: false\n208\t    reward_gaming_detected: false\n209\t    valid_bonus_vs_task_ratio: 4.2:10 (per episode)\n210\t    action_is_valid_improvement: +17pp vs vanilla\n211\t  result_rationale: Episode-level 下 dense reward gaming 不发生（与 exp013f 对比，D056 insight\n212\t    正确）。action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72-85%，模型确实学到了更多合法 action format。但 success rate\n213\t    仍 plateau 在 25%——更多 valid actions ≠ 更好的 task strategy。模型能输出合法格式但不知道 WHICH valid\n214\t    action 能推进 task。Valid action bonus 解决的是 syntax 问题而非 semantics 问题。Plateau 未突破因为瓶颈不在\n215\t    action validity 而在 credit assignment granularity（GAE 结果已证明）。\n216\t  tables: []\n217\t  figures_description:\n218\t  - 'Fig: action_is_valid 稳步上升（55%→85%），success_rate 保持 flat（25%±3pp）。两条线 decouple\n219\t    证明 valid format ≠ task success。'\n220\t  analysis: D056 insight 部分正确（episode-level 不 game dense reward），但 plateau 不是 action_is_valid\n221\t    造成的。Base agent 学会了 'speak the right language' 但不知道 'say the right thing'。Plateau\n222\t    本质是 episode-level credit 太粗——all valid actions 获得相同 reinforcement signal，模型无法区分哪个\n223\t    valid action 更好。\n224\t- name: Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\n225\t  plan_id: plan_004\n226\t  description: Per-window advantage logging 验证 sign misattribution 机制。\n227\t  expected_results:\n228\t    sign_vs_outcome_correlation: 0.72\n229\t    sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: 0.28\n230\t    gamma_k_magnitude_decay_r2: 0.45\n231\t    episode_level_advantage_variance: 0.0\n232\t    success_episodes_all_positive: 0.85\n233\t    failure_episodes_all_negative: 0.78\n234\t    mixed_sign_episodes_pct: 0.18\n235\t  result_rationale: Worst 档下 sign misattribution 存在但非 dominant。sign_vs_outcome_correlation=0.72\n236\t    说明 advantage sign 确实偏向 episode outcome，但 0.72 远非 'near 1.0' 的理论预测。28% 的 local\n237\t    quality correlation 说明 advantage 中有 non-trivial 的 local signal（GRPO 的 group normalization\n238\t    引入了组内相对排序信息）。18% 的 episodes 出现 mixed signs（部分 window positive 部分 negative in same\n239\t    episode），这不符合 'pure sign misattribution' 理论（理论预测应为 0%）。γ^k decay R²=0.45 说明 magnitude\n240\t    确实随 position 衰减但 fit 不好（noise 大）。总结：mechanism 存在但不 clean，empirical evidence 是\n241\t    'moderate support' 而非 'strong confirmation'。\n242\t  tables:\n243\t  - name: 'Table 4: Advantage sign analysis'\n244\t    columns:\n245\t    - metric\n246\t    - theoretical_prediction\n247\t    - observed\n248\t    - interpretation\n249\t    rows:\n250\t    - - sign-outcome corr\n251\t      - '>0.95'\n252\t      - '0.72'\n253\t      - Exists but not dominant\n254\t    - - sign-local_quality corr\n255\t      - <0.1\n256\t      - '0.28'\n257\t      - Non-trivial local signal present\n258\t    - - γ^k decay R²\n259\t      - '>0.8'\n260\t      - '0.45'\n261\t      - Weak fit\n262\t    - - mixed-sign episodes\n263\t      - 0%\n264\t      - 18%\n265\t      - Theory violation\n266\t    - - episode-level variance\n267\t      - '0'\n268\t      - '0'\n269\t      - Confirmed (trivially)\n270\t  figures_description:\n271\t  - 'Fig 2 draft: scatter plot of per-window advantage sign vs episode outcome. 明显\n272\t    trend 但大量 noise。不像理论预测的 clean two-cluster separation。'\n273\t  analysis: Sign misattribution 是 real phenomenon 但 paper 需要大幅 soften claims。不能写 'advantage\n274\t    sign is entirely determined by episode outcome'——实际只有 72% correlation。Mixed-sign\n275\t    episodes 的存在说明 GRPO group normalization 引入了组内 local ranking 信号（当 group 中有 partial\n276\t    success 时）。Reviewer 会 attack：'your mechanism is one factor among several, not\n277\t    THE explanation'。这把论文从 'mechanistic explanation paper' 降级为 'we observed a contributing\n278\t    factor'。\n279\t- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n280\t  plan_id: plan_005\n281\t  description: 从 exp029 checkpoints 收集 verification 后 action change 统计。\n282\t  expected_results:\n283\t    action_change_rate: 0.35\n284\t    confirmatory_rate: 0.65\n285\t    action_change_success_correlation: 0.08\n286\t    action_change_rate_success_episodes: 0.38\n287\t    action_change_rate_failure_episodes: 0.34\n288\t    per_task_variance: 'high (pick: 0.25, clean: 0.45, heat: 0.30)'\n289\t  result_rationale: Base agent 只有 28% success rate，大部分 verification 是在失败 trajectory\n290\t    中进行的。Action change rate 35%（不是 >60% confirmatory 的预期？ 其实是——65% confirmatory 符合假设）。但关键问题：action_change_success_correlation\n291\t    极低（0.08），说明 action change 与 episode success 几乎无关。在成功 episodes 中 change rate=38%，失败中=34%——差异\n292\t    negligible。这意味着 action-change 作为 reward signal 没有 information content：改变 action\n293\t    并不 predictive of 成功。原因：base agent 太弱（28% success），它的 verification 大多是 random perturbation\n294\t    而非 informed correction。\n295\t  tables: []\n296\t  figures_description:\n297\t  - 'Fig: action_change_rate 按 task type 分解。High variance across types 但 none 显示 strong\n298\t    change-success correlation。'\n299\t  analysis: Action-change reward 的前提假设（'change = informative verification'）在这个 agent\n300\t    能力水平下不成立。28% success 的 agent 做 verification 更像是 random re-sampling 而非 informed\n301\t    decision revision。Selective verification 的整个 Phase B 建立在沙子上——你需要一个足够强的 agent（≥50%\n302\t    success?）才能让 verification 成为 meaningful signal 而非 noise。\n303\t- name: Selective verification implementation\n304\t  plan_id: plan_006\n305\t  description: 实现 binary verify/skip decision。Code-only。\n306\t  expected_results:\n307\t    implementation_complete: true\n308\t    code_lines_added: 280\n309\t    integration_test_pass: true\n310\t    gpu_hours: 0\n311\t  result_rationale: 纯代码实现，无 ML 依赖。能完成但实际 training（plan_007）会 fail 因为 base agent 太弱。\n312\t  tables: []\n313\t  figures_description: []\n314\t  analysis: Implementation 本身 trivial。问题不在代码而在 downstream training signal quality。\n315\t- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n316\t  plan_id: plan_007\n317\t  description: 从 exp029 best checkpoint 训练 selective verification policy。\n318\t  expected_results:\n319\t    verification_rate: 0.88\n320\t    success_rate: 0.219\n321\t    success_delta_vs_always_on_pp: -6.2\n322\t    cost_reduction: 0.12\n323\t    training_converged: false\n324\t    policy_behavior: near-always-verify (degenerate)\n325\t  result_rationale: Base agent 只有 28% success。Selective policy 面临两个问题：(1) action-change\n326\t    reward 无 information content（plan_005 证明 change 与 success 无关），所以 reward signal\n327\t    is noise；(2) skip verification 有 immediate cost（performance drop），而 base agent\n328\t    已经很弱，任何 skip 都大幅降低本就脆弱的 success rate。Policy 学到 degenerate solution：几乎 always verify（88%\n329\t    rate），偶尔 skip 是 random noise 而非 learned strategy。12% cost reduction 远未达到 40% target。Success\n330\t    还 drop 了 6pp 因为那 12% skip 确实 hurt。\n331\t  tables:\n332\t  - name: 'Table 5: B-IAVR training results'\n333\t    columns:\n334\t    - metric\n335\t    - target\n336\t    - achieved\n337\t    - gap\n338\t    rows:\n339\t    - - verification_rate_reduction\n340\t      - ≥40%\n341\t      - 12%\n342\t      - -28pp\n343\t    - - success_delta_vs_always_on\n344\t      - <5pp\n345\t      - -6.2pp\n346\t      - Fail\n347\t    - - cost_reduction_pct\n348\t      - ≥40%\n349\t      - 12%\n350\t      - -28pp\n351\t    - - policy_entropy_final\n352\t      - '>0.3'\n353\t      - '0.08'\n354\t      - Collapsed to always-verify\n355\t  figures_description:\n356\t  - 'Fig: verification rate 从 100% 缓慢下降到 88% 然后 plateau。Policy entropy → 0 表明 degenerate\n357\t    convergence。'\n358\t  analysis: Selective verification 在 base agent success < 30% 时完全不可行。Policy 无法学到 meaningful\n359\t    skip pattern 因为：(1) reward signal (action-change) 是 noise，(2) skipping has guaranteed\n360\t    downside with no upside at this performance level。整个 Phase B contribution 不成立。\n361\t- name: Selective verification full comparison\n362\t  plan_id: plan_008\n363\t  description: Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold 对比。\n364\t  expected_results:\n365\t    always_on_success: 0.281\n366\t    biavr_success: 0.219\n367\t    biavr_verification_rate: 0.88\n368\t    no_verify_success: 0.188\n369\t    random_p05_success: 0.234\n370\t    random_p05_verification_rate: 0.5\n371\t    confidence_threshold_success: 0.25\n372\t    confidence_threshold_verification_rate: 0.62\n373\t  result_rationale: 'B-IAVR 不 dominate Pareto frontier。Random-p=0.5 在 success/cost\n374\t    tradeoff 上 comparable to B-IAVR（random: 23.4% success at 50% cost vs B-IAVR: 21.9%\n375\t    at 88% cost）——random 更 cost-efficient。Confidence threshold 也优于 B-IAVR。这证明 learned\n376\t    policy 不优于 naive baselines，因为 base agent 太弱导致所有 verification 策略 degenerate。No-verify\n377\t    只 drop 9pp（远低于预期的 ≥10pp），说明 verification 本身 value 也有限。'\n378\t  tables:\n379\t  - name: 'Table 6: Verification strategy comparison'\n380\t    columns:\n381\t    - method\n382\t    - success\n383\t    - verify_rate\n384\t    - cost_tokens\n385\t    - success_per_token\n386\t    rows:\n387\t    - - always-on\n388\t      - 28.1%\n389\t      - 100%\n390\t      - 1.00x\n391\t      - '0.281'\n392\t    - - B-IAVR (ours)\n393\t      - 21.9%\n394\t      - 88%\n395\t      - 0.92x\n396\t      - '0.238'\n397\t    - - random-p=0.5\n398\t      - 23.4%\n399\t      - 50%\n400\t      - 0.67x\n401\t      - '0.349'\n402\t    - - confidence\n403\t      - 25.0%\n404\t      - 62%\n405\t      - 0.74x\n406\t      - '0.338'\n407\t    - - no-verify\n408\t      - 18.8%\n409\t      - 0%\n410\t      - 0.45x\n411\t      - '0.418'\n412\t  figures_description:\n413\t  - 'Fig: Pareto frontier (success vs cost). B-IAVR 位于 frontier 内部（dominated by random-p\n414\t    and confidence）。No-verify 有最好的 tokens-per-success efficiency。'\n415\t  analysis: Paper Claim 3 完全 fail。B-IAVR 被 naive baselines dominate。讽刺的是 no-verify\n416\t    的 efficiency 最高（per-token success ratio），说明在 28% success 水平下，verification 本身就是\n417\t    pure overhead——agent 改变 action 不提升 success。\n418\t- name: No-verify ablation\n419\t  plan_id: plan_009\n420\t  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。\n421\t  expected_results:\n422\t    success_rate: 0.188\n423\t    action_is_valid: 0.52\n424\t    delta_vs_always_on: -9.3\n425\t  result_rationale: No-verify 只 drop ~9pp（28.1% → 18.8%），低于预期的 ≥10pp。原因：在 28% success\n426\t    level，verification 的 marginal value 有限——agent 的 success 主要来自偶然走对 path，verification\n427\t    只是小幅增加 correction 机会但不 fundamentally 改变 strategy。如果 base agent 更强（如 GAE 的 44%），verification\n428\t    drop 可能更大，但我们无法测试因为 episode-level 训练不出更强的 agent。\n429\t  tables: []\n430\t  figures_description: []\n431\t  analysis: Verification value 存在但 modest（9pp）。不足以支撑 'selective verification 是重要 research\n432\t    problem' 的 motivation——reviewer 会说 'if verification only adds 9pp, why not just\n433\t    skip it entirely and save tokens?'\n434\t- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n435\t  plan_id: plan_010\n436\t  description: Stratify by policy entropy，测试 action-change-success correlation 是否\n437\t    holds。\n438\t  expected_results:\n439\t    partial_correlation_after_entropy_control: 0.03\n440\t    p_value: 0.42\n441\t    low_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.05\n442\t    high_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.11\n443\t    entropy_success_correlation: -0.15\n444\t  result_rationale: Controlling for entropy 后 action-change-success correlation 从\n445\t    0.08 降至 0.03（p=0.42，not significant）。这证明 plan_005 中观察到的微弱 correlation 完全由 entropy\n446\t    confound 解释：高 entropy → 更多 random action change + 更低 success。Action change 本身无\n447\t    causal relationship with success。Reviewer concern 'action change = noise' 被证实。\n448\t  tables: []\n449\t  figures_description:\n450\t  - 'Fig: partial correlation heatmap across entropy strata. All cells near zero after\n451\t    controlling.'\n452\t  analysis: Action-change 作为 verification informativeness proxy 的理论基础被否定。Change 只是\n453\t    high entropy 的 side effect，不是 'verification found better action'。Claim 2 的 reward\n454\t    design 无 empirical grounding。\n455\t- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n456\t  plan_id: plan_011\n457\t  description: Inject random action changes at same rate，对比 verification-triggered。\n458\t  expected_results:\n459\t    success_rate_verification_triggered: 0.22\n460\t    success_rate_random_change: 0.19\n461\t    delta_pp: 3.0\n462\t    p_value: 0.31\n463\t    effect_size_cohens_d: 0.12\n464\t  result_rationale: Verification-triggered changes 只比 random changes 好 3pp（not significant,\n465\t    p=0.31）。Effect size tiny (d=0.12)。原因：28% success 的 agent 做 verification 时，其 'correction'\n466\t    几乎等价于 random re-sampling from policy——agent 没有真正的 'second opinion' 能力，verification\n467\t    output 和 original output 来自同一个 weak policy distribution。Causal evidence for verification\n468\t    value 不成立。\n469\t  tables: []\n470\t  figures_description:\n471\t  - 'Fig: success rate comparison with 95% CI error bars. Bars overlap heavily.'\n472\t  analysis: Verification 在 weak agent 上 ≈ random perturbation。这是 Claim 2 的 death blow——不仅\n473\t    action-change 不是好 reward（plan_010），verification 本身在当前 agent 能力下就没有 causal value（它的\n474\t    correction 不比 random good）。\n475\t- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n476\t  plan_id: plan_012\n477\t  description: 比较不同 reward signals 训练 selective policy。\n478\t  expected_results:\n479\t    action_change_success: 0.219\n480\t    action_change_verify_rate: 0.88\n481\t    random_trigger_success: 0.234\n482\t    random_trigger_verify_rate: 0.52\n483\t    confidence_reward_success: 0.25\n484\t    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 0.65\n485\t  result_rationale: 所有 reward variants 都 fail 达到 target，但 action-change 是最差的——它训出\n486\t    near-always-verify 因为 reward signal 是 noise（plan_010 已证明）。Random trigger 反而学到\n487\t    reasonable skip rate 因为 random reward 至少不 mislead（均匀分布）。Confidence 略好因为 confidence\n488\t    与 success 有 weak correlation。讽刺：learned reward (action-change) 输给了 uninformed\n489\t    baselines。\n490\t  tables:\n491\t  - name: 'Table 7: Reward signal comparison'\n492\t    columns:\n493\t    - reward_type\n494\t    - success\n495\t    - verify_rate\n496\t    - pareto_dominated\n497\t    rows:\n498\t    - - action-change (ours)\n499\t      - 21.9%\n500\t      - 88%\n501\t      - Yes (by all others)\n502\t    - - random trigger\n503\t      - 23.4%\n504\t      - 52%\n505\t      - 'No'\n506\t    - - confidence-based\n507\t      - 25.0%\n508\t      - 65%\n509\t      - 'No'\n510\t  figures_description: []\n511\t  analysis: Action-change reward 是 worst performer。Claim 2 ('action-change is effective\n512\t    intrinsic reward') 被彻底 falsified。Paper 失去了 selective verification 的 technical\n513\t    contribution。\n514\t- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n515\t  plan_id: plan_013\n516\t  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router, head-to-head 对比。\n517\t  expected_results:\n518\t    ares_success: 0.25\n519\t    ares_verification_rate: 0.55\n520\t    ares_cost_reduction: 0.38\n521\t    biavr_success: 0.219\n522\t    biavr_verification_rate: 0.88\n523\t    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.12\n524\t    ares_dominates_biavr: true\n525\t  result_rationale: ARES 用 SFT 从 oracle decisions 学 router，不需要 RL reward signal quality。在\n526\t    same base agent 上 ARES 能学到 55% verification rate 且保持 success（因为它直接学 'when did\n527\t    verification change outcome' from data），而 B-IAVR 依赖 noisy RL reward 学不到 meaningful\n528\t    policy。ARES 在 Pareto frontier 上 dominate B-IAVR。我们不仅没有 '≥10pp better cost reduction'，反而被\n529\t    dominated。\n530\t  tables: []\n531\t  figures_description:\n532\t  - 'Fig: Pareto frontier with ARES point clearly dominating B-IAVR point.'\n533\t  analysis: SFT approach (ARES) 优于 RL approach (B-IAVR) 在这个 setting 下。原因：SFT 有 oracle\n534\t    supervision（从 data 直接学 when to verify），不受 reward noise 影响。RL 需要 good reward signal\n535\t    但我们没有。Paper 的 'RL > SFT for selective verification' implicit claim 被反驳。\n536\t- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n537\t  plan_id: plan_014\n538\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。\n539\t  expected_results:\n540\t    episode_level_success: 0.15\n541\t    step_independent_success: 0.12\n542\t    ratio: 1.25\n543\t    episode_level_std: 0.06\n544\t    step_independent_std: 0.08\n545\t    difference_significant: false\n546\t    p_value: 0.38\n547\t  result_rationale: Worst 档下 scienceworld_episode_vs_step_ratio 在 [0.8, 1.5]。Ratio=1.25\n548\t    意味着 episode-level 只是 marginally better（15% vs 12%，差异 3pp not significant p=0.38）。ScienceWorld\n549\t    有更短的 episodes（~10-15 steps vs ALFWorld 30-50），所以 step-independent 的 information\n550\t    loss 没那么严重——shorter episodes = fewer windows = less sign misattribution。这反驳了 'episode-level\n551\t    universally superior' claim，支持 'advantage depends on episode length' 的 nuanced\n552\t    view，但也意味着我们的 contribution 是 domain-specific 而非 general。\n553\t  tables:\n554\t  - name: 'Table 8: ScienceWorld transfer'\n555\t    columns:\n556\t    - method\n557\t    - success\n558\t    - std\n559\t    - avg_episode_length\n560\t    rows:\n561\t    - - episode-level\n562\t      - 15.0%\n563\t      - 6pp\n564\t      - 12.3 steps\n565\t    - - step-independent (h=5)\n566\t      - 12.0%\n567\t      - 8pp\n568\t      - 12.3 steps\n569\t  figures_description: []\n570\t  analysis: 'Episode-level advantage 不 generalize to shorter-horizon tasks。ScienceWorld\n571\t    的短 episode 使 step-independent 的缺陷不 manifest。Reviewer concern #5 (single environment)\n572\t    被证实——our finding is ALFWorld-specific (long horizon)，不是 general principle。'\n573\t- name: 7B model scaling verification\n574\t  plan_id: plan_015\n575\t  description: Qwen3-7B 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent。\n576\t  expected_results:\n577\t    episode_level_7b_success: 0.35\n578\t    step_independent_7b_success: 0.22\n579\t    delta_pp: 13\n580\t    relative_improvement: 1.59\n581\t    step_independent_collapse: false\n582\t    step_independent_7b_h5_success: 0.18\n583\t  result_rationale: 7B 模型更强，step-independent 不完全崩溃（22% vs 1.7B 的 0%）。原因：更大模型有更好的 in-context\n584\t    learning，即使 h=5 窗口也能从有限 context 推断 partial strategy。Episode-level 仍优（35% vs 22%）但\n585\t    gap 缩小（13pp vs 1.7B 的 28pp）。这进一步削弱 'catastrophic failure' narrative——在 stronger\n586\t    model 上 step-independent 只是 suboptimal 而非 catastrophic。Reviewer 会问 'at what model\n587\t    size does the gap disappear entirely?'\n588\t  tables:\n589\t  - name: 'Table 9: 7B scaling'\n590\t    columns:\n591\t    - method\n592\t    - 1.7B\n593\t    - 7B\n594\t    - gap_reduction\n595\t    rows:\n596\t    - - episode-level\n597\t      - 28.1%\n598\t      - 35%\n599\t      - —\n600\t    - - step-independent (h=5)\n601\t      - 0%\n602\t      - 22%\n603\t      - 'Gap: 28pp→13pp'\n604\t  figures_description: []\n605\t  analysis: Episode-level advantage diminishes with model scale。7B step-independent\n606\t    不崩溃（22%），gap 缩小到 13pp。暗示 'catastrophic failure' 是 small model + long horizon 的特定\n607\t    interaction，更大模型的 in-context learning 能部分补偿 credit assignment 缺陷。Paper 的 alarm\n608\t    ('step-independent catastrophically fails!') 变成了 'step-independent is suboptimal\n609\t    for small models on long tasks'——much weaker claim。\n610\t- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n611\t  plan_id: plan_016\n612\t  description: 按 ALFWorld task type 分解 success。\n613\t  expected_results:\n614\t    pick_success: 0.35\n615\t    clean_success: 0.25\n616\t    heat_success: 0.3\n617\t    cool_success: 0.2\n618\t    examine_success: 0.15\n619\t    pick_two_success: 0.1\n620\t    episode_length_correlation: 0.45\n621\t    longest_task_success: 0.1\n622\t    shortest_task_success: 0.35\n623\t  result_rationale: '较短 task（pick: ~15 steps）success 较高（35%），较长 task（pick_two: ~45\n624\t    steps, examine: ~40 steps）success 最低（10-15%）。Episode length correlation=0.45 (moderate)。这\n625\t    partially 支持 ''longer tasks benefit more from episode-level''，但 correlation 不够\n626\t    strong——其他 factors（task complexity, number of required objects）也 matter。Not a\n627\t    clean story。'\n628\t  tables:\n629\t  - name: 'Table 10: Per-task breakdown'\n630\t    columns:\n631\t    - task_type\n632\t    - success\n633\t    - avg_episode_length\n634\t    - step_indep_success\n635\t    rows:\n636\t    - - pick\n637\t      - 35%\n638\t      - '15'\n639\t      - 8%\n640\t    - - heat\n641\t      - 30%\n642\t      - '22'\n643\t      - 3%\n644\t    - - clean\n645\t      - 25%\n646\t      - '28'\n647\t      - 0%\n648\t    - - cool\n649\t      - 20%\n650\t      - '25'\n651\t      - 2%\n652\t    - - examine\n653\t      - 15%\n654\t      - '38'\n655\t      - 0%\n656\t    - - pick_two\n657\t      - 10%\n658\t      - '45'\n659\t      - 0%\n660\t  figures_description:\n661\t  - 'Fig: scatter plot success vs episode_length, with moderate negative trend (r=-0.45).'\n662\t  analysis: Task length 是 contributing factor 但非唯一因素。Paper 可以 claim 'longer tasks\n663\t    benefit more' 但不能 claim 'length is the mechanism'。Adds nuance but not a strong\n664\t    independent contribution。\n665\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbfaf1eb-86b3-4c62-a538-5d4d55066586","uuid":"ff9b5c13-04e7-443c-bc52-45c2c7b0f695","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:15:23.056Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T133129/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 原始 framing 的两个支柱均不成立：(1) 'episode-level 就够了' 被 GAE 大幅超越反驳（finer\n  credit 确实必要），(2) 'catastrophic failure at small h' 被不一致的 h-sweep 削弱（部分 seed h=5\n  也能学到 15-20%）。Contrarian positioning 崩塌。需要完全 reframe 为 empirical taxonomy 或 sufficient\n  conditions 研究。Selective verification 因 base agent 太弱（<30%）完全不可行。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Context window h-sweep ablation (3 seeds each)\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: Sweep h={2, 5, 10, 20, full}, 15 steps, 3 seeds each. 测试 credit assignment\n    cliff 是否 robust。\n  expected_results:\n    h2_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.0\n    h2_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.031\n    h2_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.0\n    h5_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.156\n    h5_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.0\n    h5_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.188\n    h10_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.094\n    h10_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.219\n    h10_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.125\n    h20_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.188\n    h20_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.25\n    h20_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.156\n    full_seed1_val_success_step15: 0.25\n    full_seed2_val_success_step15: 0.281\n    full_seed3_val_success_step15: 0.219\n    collapse_rate_h2: 0.67\n    collapse_rate_h5: 0.33\n    collapse_rate_h10: 0.0\n    cliff_threshold_range: 3-8 (seed-dependent)\n  result_rationale: Worst 档下 h-sweep cliff 不一致。h=2 多数 seed 崩溃但非全部（seed2 靠运气学到少量 pattern）。h=5\n    更关键：seed1/3 没有崩溃且学到 15-19%，只有 seed2 崩溃。这直接削弱 'catastrophic failure below threshold'\n    narrative——cliff 位置是 stochastic 的，不是 deterministic 的。h=10/20/full 之间差异不大（均在 10-25%\n    区间），说明即使给了足够 context，episode-level 本身也有天花板。Monotonic degradation 假设不成立：h=5 的某些\n    seed 可以接近 h=full。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: h-sweep results (mean ± std across 3 seeds)'\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - val_success_mean\n    - val_success_std\n    - collapse_rate\n    - convergence_step\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 1.0%\n      - 1.8%\n      - 67%\n      - 3-4\n    - - 5\n      - 11.5%\n      - 10.4%\n      - 33%\n      - 4-6\n    - - 10\n      - 14.6%\n      - 6.3%\n      - 0%\n      - N/A\n    - - 20\n      - 19.8%\n      - 4.8%\n      - 0%\n      - N/A\n    - - full\n      - 25.0%\n      - 3.1%\n      - 0%\n      - N/A\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: h-value vs val_success with per-seed lines. 无 clean cliff——h=5 区间有巨大 variance\n    band（0-19%），与 h=10 overlap。Error bars 在 h=5 处最宽。'\n  analysis: Cliff 不 robust。h=5 std=10.4pp 意味着 cliff 位置是 random variable 而非 structural\n    property。无法 claim 'h<X catastrophically fails' 因为 X 取决于 seed。这削弱了 paper 的核心 figure\n    说服力——reviewer 会问 'with more seeds would the cliff disappear entirely?'\n- name: Multi-seed replication (5 seeds total)\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 4 additional seeds for exp029 episode-level config, report mean ± std。\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_val_success_step15: 0.281\n    seed2_val_success_step15: 0.188\n    seed3_val_success_step15: 0.313\n    seed4_val_success_step15: 0.156\n    seed5_val_success_step15: 0.25\n    mean_val_success: 0.238\n    std_val_success: 0.062\n    max_val_success_any_seed: 0.313\n    min_val_success_any_seed: 0.156\n    seeds_above_30pct: 1\n    seeds_below_20pct: 1\n    convergence_step_range: 10-15 (all plateau)\n    step50_mean_val_success: 0.26\n    step50_std: 0.071\n  result_rationale: Worst 档要求 multi_seed_std > 8pp。5 seeds 中 std=6.2pp（接近但略低于阈值），但如果看\n    step 50（训练更久），seed 4 可能进一步恶化（plateau 后缓慢下降到 12-15%），使得 late-stage std 达到 8-10pp。关键问题：seed\n    4 只有 15.6%，与 step-independent h=10 的 best seed（21.9%）重叠——episode-level 的 advantage\n    over step-independent 在 per-seed 层面不 universal。reproducibility 不够 strong（CI 太宽），reviewer\n    会 flag 'your method might just be getting lucky on some seeds'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level GRPO results'\n    columns:\n    - seed\n    - step5_val\n    - step10_val\n    - step15_val\n    - step50_val\n    - plateau_onset\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 25.0%\n      - 25.0%\n      - 28.1%\n      - 28.1%\n      - step 10\n    - - 2\n      - 18.8%\n      - 18.8%\n      - 18.8%\n      - 21.9%\n      - step 5\n    - - 3\n      - 25.0%\n      - 31.3%\n      - 31.3%\n      - 31.3%\n      - step 10\n    - - 4\n      - 12.5%\n      - 15.6%\n      - 15.6%\n      - 15.6%\n      - step 5\n    - - 5\n      - 18.8%\n      - 25.0%\n      - 25.0%\n      - 28.1%\n      - step 10\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Training curves (5 seeds) with shaded std band. Band 宽度在 step 5 后稳定但 wide（±6pp），所有\n    seed 在 step 10-15 plateau，无 seed 突破 32%。'\n  analysis: Mean 23.8% ± 6.2pp。95% CI = [11.3%, 36.3%]。这个 CI 与 step-independent h=10\n    mean（14.6%）有 overlap，削弱 episode-level 的统计 significance。更致命的是 plateau 现象——所有 seed\n    在 step 10-15 停滞，额外训练 35 步几乎无改善，说明 episode-level GRPO 本身有信息瓶颈（无 per-token credit）。\n- name: GAE baseline comparison\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps\n    × 3 seeds。\n  expected_results:\n    gae_095_mean_val_success_step15: 0.438\n    gae_095_std: 0.047\n    gae_100_mean_val_success_step15: 0.375\n    gae_100_std: 0.055\n    episode_grpo_mean_val_success_step15: 0.238\n    gae_095_vs_episode_delta_pp: 20.0\n    gae_100_vs_episode_delta_pp: 13.7\n    gae_095_action_is_valid: 0.78\n    gae_095_convergence_step: 12\n    gae_still_improving_at_step15: true\n  result_rationale: Worst 档核心假设：GAE >> episode-level GRPO（delta > 15pp）。GAE(0.95)\n    有 value function 做 per-token credit assignment，能区分 trajectory 中好/坏 action 并精确更新。Episode-level\n    GRPO 所有 token 共享一个 advantage（相当于 REINFORCE），缺乏 temporal difference 信息。20pp gap\n    证明 per-token credit 是关键——episode-level 'just knowing the outcome' 不够，你需要知道 which\n    tokens contributed。这直接反驳 paper 的 contrarian claim 'coarser is better'。GAE(1.0,1.0)\n    稍弱因为 high variance（相当于 Monte Carlo），但仍优于 GRPO 因为 critic 提供 baseline。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: GAE vs Episode-level GRPO'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - val_success_mean\n    - std\n    - delta_vs_episode_grpo\n    - action_is_valid\n    - still_improving\n    rows:\n    - - Episode GRPO\n      - 23.8%\n      - 6.2pp\n      - —\n      - 55%\n      - No (plateau)\n    - - GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0)\n      - 37.5%\n      - 5.5pp\n      - +13.7pp\n      - 72%\n      - Marginal\n    - - GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0)\n      - 43.8%\n      - 4.7pp\n      - +20.0pp\n      - 78%\n      - 'Yes'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Learning curves — GAE(0.95) clearly dominates from step 5 onward, with episode\n    GRPO plateauing while GAE continues climbing. The gap widens over training.'\n  analysis: GAE 大幅超越 episode-level GRPO 证明 per-token temporal difference credit 是关键。Episode-level\n    的 'advantage sign is correct' 不够——你还需要 magnitude differentiation across tokens。这反驳了\n    contrarian positioning：社区追求 finer credit 是对的。Episode-level 只是 '方向不错但信息太粗' 的 solution。Paper\n    的核心 contribution（'coarser suffices'）被实验数据否定。\n- name: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus (plateau-breaker)\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 测试能否打破 plateau 且不 game。\n  expected_results:\n    val_success_step15: 0.25\n    val_action_is_valid_step15: 0.72\n    val_action_is_valid_step30: 0.85\n    success_plateau_broken: false\n    reward_gaming_detected: false\n    valid_bonus_vs_task_ratio: 4.2:10 (per episode)\n    action_is_valid_improvement: +17pp vs vanilla\n  result_rationale: Episode-level 下 dense reward gaming 不发生（与 exp013f 对比，D056 insight\n    正确）。action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72-85%，模型确实学到了更多合法 action format。但 success rate\n    仍 plateau 在 25%——更多 valid actions ≠ 更好的 task strategy。模型能输出合法格式但不知道 WHICH valid\n    action 能推进 task。Valid action bonus 解决的是 syntax 问题而非 semantics 问题。Plateau 未突破因为瓶颈不在\n    action validity 而在 credit assignment granularity（GAE 结果已证明）。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: action_is_valid 稳步上升（55%→85%），success_rate 保持 flat（25%±3pp）。两条线 decouple\n    证明 valid format ≠ task success。'\n  analysis: D056 insight 部分正确（episode-level 不 game dense reward），但 plateau 不是 action_is_valid\n    造成的。Base agent 学会了 'speak the right language' 但不知道 'say the right thing'。Plateau\n    本质是 episode-level credit 太粗——all valid actions 获得相同 reinforcement signal，模型无法区分哪个\n    valid action 更好。\n- name: Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: Per-window advantage logging 验证 sign misattribution 机制。\n  expected_results:\n    sign_vs_outcome_correlation: 0.72\n    sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: 0.28\n    gamma_k_magnitude_decay_r2: 0.45\n    episode_level_advantage_variance: 0.0\n    success_episodes_all_positive: 0.85\n    failure_episodes_all_negative: 0.78\n    mixed_sign_episodes_pct: 0.18\n  result_rationale: Worst 档下 sign misattribution 存在但非 dominant。sign_vs_outcome_correlation=0.72\n    说明 advantage sign 确实偏向 episode outcome，但 0.72 远非 'near 1.0' 的理论预测。28% 的 local\n    quality correlation 说明 advantage 中有 non-trivial 的 local signal（GRPO 的 group normalization\n    引入了组内相对排序信息）。18% 的 episodes 出现 mixed signs（部分 window positive 部分 negative in same\n    episode），这不符合 'pure sign misattribution' 理论（理论预测应为 0%）。γ^k decay R²=0.45 说明 magnitude\n    确实随 position 衰减但 fit 不好（noise 大）。总结：mechanism 存在但不 clean，empirical evidence 是\n    'moderate support' 而非 'strong confirmation'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: Advantage sign analysis'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - theoretical_prediction\n    - observed\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - sign-outcome corr\n      - '>0.95'\n      - '0.72'\n      - Exists but not dominant\n    - - sign-local_quality corr\n      - <0.1\n      - '0.28'\n      - Non-trivial local signal present\n    - - γ^k decay R²\n      - '>0.8'\n      - '0.45'\n      - Weak fit\n    - - mixed-sign episodes\n      - 0%\n      - 18%\n      - Theory violation\n    - - episode-level variance\n      - '0'\n      - '0'\n      - Confirmed (trivially)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 2 draft: scatter plot of per-window advantage sign vs episode outcome. 明显\n    trend 但大量 noise。不像理论预测的 clean two-cluster separation。'\n  analysis: Sign misattribution 是 real phenomenon 但 paper 需要大幅 soften claims。不能写 'advantage\n    sign is entirely determined by episode outcome'——实际只有 72% correlation。Mixed-sign\n    episodes 的存在说明 GRPO group normalization 引入了组内 local ranking 信号（当 group 中有 partial\n    success 时）。Reviewer 会 attack：'your mechanism is one factor among several, not\n    THE explanation'。这把论文从 'mechanistic explanation paper' 降级为 'we observed a contributing\n    factor'。\n- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 从 exp029 checkpoints 收集 verification 后 action change 统计。\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_rate: 0.35\n    confirmatory_rate: 0.65\n    action_change_success_correlation: 0.08\n    action_change_rate_success_episodes: 0.38\n    action_change_rate_failure_episodes: 0.34\n    per_task_variance: 'high (pick: 0.25, clean: 0.45, heat: 0.30)'\n  result_rationale: Base agent 只有 28% success rate，大部分 verification 是在失败 trajectory\n    中进行的。Action change rate 35%（不是 >60% confirmatory 的预期？ 其实是——65% confirmatory 符合假设）。但关键问题：action_change_success_correlation\n    极低（0.08），说明 action change 与 episode success 几乎无关。在成功 episodes 中 change rate=38%，失败中=34%——差异\n    negligible。这意味着 action-change 作为 reward signal 没有 information content：改变 action\n    并不 predictive of 成功。原因：base agent 太弱（28% success），它的 verification 大多是 random perturbation\n    而非 informed correction。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: action_change_rate 按 task type 分解。High variance across types 但 none 显示 strong\n    change-success correlation。'\n  analysis: Action-change reward 的前提假设（'change = informative verification'）在这个 agent\n    能力水平下不成立。28% success 的 agent 做 verification 更像是 random re-sampling 而非 informed\n    decision revision。Selective verification 的整个 Phase B 建立在沙子上——你需要一个足够强的 agent（≥50%\n    success?）才能让 verification 成为 meaningful signal 而非 noise。\n- name: Selective verification implementation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 实现 binary verify/skip decision。Code-only。\n  expected_results:\n    implementation_complete: true\n    code_lines_added: 280\n    integration_test_pass: true\n    gpu_hours: 0\n  result_rationale: 纯代码实现，无 ML 依赖。能完成但实际 training（plan_007）会 fail 因为 base agent 太弱。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Implementation 本身 trivial。问题不在代码而在 downstream training signal quality。\n- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 从 exp029 best checkpoint 训练 selective verification policy。\n  expected_results:\n    verification_rate: 0.88\n    success_rate: 0.219\n    success_delta_vs_always_on_pp: -6.2\n    cost_reduction: 0.12\n    training_converged: false\n    policy_behavior: near-always-verify (degenerate)\n  result_rationale: Base agent 只有 28% success。Selective policy 面临两个问题：(1) action-change\n    reward 无 information content（plan_005 证明 change 与 success 无关），所以 reward signal\n    is noise；(2) skip verification 有 immediate cost（performance drop），而 base agent\n    已经很弱，任何 skip 都大幅降低本就脆弱的 success rate。Policy 学到 degenerate solution：几乎 always verify（88%\n    rate），偶尔 skip 是 random noise 而非 learned strategy。12% cost reduction 远未达到 40% target。Success\n    还 drop 了 6pp 因为那 12% skip 确实 hurt。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: B-IAVR training results'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - target\n    - achieved\n    - gap\n    rows:\n    - - verification_rate_reduction\n      - ≥40%\n      - 12%\n      - -28pp\n    - - success_delta_vs_always_on\n      - <5pp\n      - -6.2pp\n      - Fail\n    - - cost_reduction_pct\n      - ≥40%\n      - 12%\n      - -28pp\n    - - policy_entropy_final\n      - '>0.3'\n      - '0.08'\n      - Collapsed to always-verify\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: verification rate 从 100% 缓慢下降到 88% 然后 plateau。Policy entropy → 0 表明 degenerate\n    convergence。'\n  analysis: Selective verification 在 base agent success < 30% 时完全不可行。Policy 无法学到 meaningful\n    skip pattern 因为：(1) reward signal (action-change) 是 noise，(2) skipping has guaranteed\n    downside with no upside at this performance level。整个 Phase B contribution 不成立。\n- name: Selective verification full comparison\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold 对比。\n  expected_results:\n    always_on_success: 0.281\n    biavr_success: 0.219\n    biavr_verification_rate: 0.88\n    no_verify_success: 0.188\n    random_p05_success: 0.234\n    random_p05_verification_rate: 0.5\n    confidence_threshold_success: 0.25\n    confidence_threshold_verification_rate: 0.62\n  result_rationale: 'B-IAVR 不 dominate Pareto frontier。Random-p=0.5 在 success/cost\n    tradeoff 上 comparable to B-IAVR（random: 23.4% success at 50% cost vs B-IAVR: 21.9%\n    at 88% cost）——random 更 cost-efficient。Confidence threshold 也优于 B-IAVR。这证明 learned\n    policy 不优于 naive baselines，因为 base agent 太弱导致所有 verification 策略 degenerate。No-verify\n    只 drop 9pp（远低于预期的 ≥10pp），说明 verification 本身 value 也有限。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Verification strategy comparison'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - cost_tokens\n    - success_per_token\n    rows:\n    - - always-on\n      - 28.1%\n      - 100%\n      - 1.00x\n      - '0.281'\n    - - B-IAVR (ours)\n      - 21.9%\n      - 88%\n      - 0.92x\n      - '0.238'\n    - - random-p=0.5\n      - 23.4%\n      - 50%\n      - 0.67x\n      - '0.349'\n    - - confidence\n      - 25.0%\n      - 62%\n      - 0.74x\n      - '0.338'\n    - - no-verify\n      - 18.8%\n      - 0%\n      - 0.45x\n      - '0.418'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Pareto frontier (success vs cost). B-IAVR 位于 frontier 内部（dominated by random-p\n    and confidence）。No-verify 有最好的 tokens-per-success efficiency。'\n  analysis: Paper Claim 3 完全 fail。B-IAVR 被 naive baselines dominate。讽刺的是 no-verify\n    的 efficiency 最高（per-token success ratio），说明在 28% success 水平下，verification 本身就是\n    pure overhead——agent 改变 action 不提升 success。\n- name: No-verify ablation\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。\n  expected_results:\n    success_rate: 0.188\n    action_is_valid: 0.52\n    delta_vs_always_on: -9.3\n  result_rationale: No-verify 只 drop ~9pp（28.1% → 18.8%），低于预期的 ≥10pp。原因：在 28% success\n    level，verification 的 marginal value 有限——agent 的 success 主要来自偶然走对 path，verification\n    只是小幅增加 correction 机会但不 fundamentally 改变 strategy。如果 base agent 更强（如 GAE 的 44%），verification\n    drop 可能更大，但我们无法测试因为 episode-level 训练不出更强的 agent。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Verification value 存在但 modest（9pp）。不足以支撑 'selective verification 是重要 research\n    problem' 的 motivation——reviewer 会说 'if verification only adds 9pp, why not just\n    skip it entirely and save tokens?'\n- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Stratify by policy entropy，测试 action-change-success correlation 是否\n    holds。\n  expected_results:\n    partial_correlation_after_entropy_control: 0.03\n    p_value: 0.42\n    low_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.05\n    high_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.11\n    entropy_success_correlation: -0.15\n  result_rationale: Controlling for entropy 后 action-change-success correlation 从\n    0.08 降至 0.03（p=0.42，not significant）。这证明 plan_005 中观察到的微弱 correlation 完全由 entropy\n    confound 解释：高 entropy → 更多 random action change + 更低 success。Action change 本身无\n    causal relationship with success。Reviewer concern 'action change = noise' 被证实。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: partial correlation heatmap across entropy strata. All cells near zero after\n    controlling.'\n  analysis: Action-change 作为 verification informativeness proxy 的理论基础被否定。Change 只是\n    high entropy 的 side effect，不是 'verification found better action'。Claim 2 的 reward\n    design 无 empirical grounding。\n- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: Inject random action changes at same rate，对比 verification-triggered。\n  expected_results:\n    success_rate_verification_triggered: 0.22\n    success_rate_random_change: 0.19\n    delta_pp: 3.0\n    p_value: 0.31\n    effect_size_cohens_d: 0.12\n  result_rationale: Verification-triggered changes 只比 random changes 好 3pp（not significant,\n    p=0.31）。Effect size tiny (d=0.12)。原因：28% success 的 agent 做 verification 时，其 'correction'\n    几乎等价于 random re-sampling from policy——agent 没有真正的 'second opinion' 能力，verification\n    output 和 original output 来自同一个 weak policy distribution。Causal evidence for verification\n    value 不成立。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: success rate comparison with 95% CI error bars. Bars overlap heavily.'\n  analysis: Verification 在 weak agent 上 ≈ random perturbation。这是 Claim 2 的 death blow——不仅\n    action-change 不是好 reward（plan_010），verification 本身在当前 agent 能力下就没有 causal value（它的\n    correction 不比 random good）。\n- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 比较不同 reward signals 训练 selective policy。\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_success: 0.219\n    action_change_verify_rate: 0.88\n    random_trigger_success: 0.234\n    random_trigger_verify_rate: 0.52\n    confidence_reward_success: 0.25\n    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 0.65\n  result_rationale: 所有 reward variants 都 fail 达到 target，但 action-change 是最差的——它训出\n    near-always-verify 因为 reward signal 是 noise（plan_010 已证明）。Random trigger 反而学到\n    reasonable skip rate 因为 random reward 至少不 mislead（均匀分布）。Confidence 略好因为 confidence\n    与 success 有 weak correlation。讽刺：learned reward (action-change) 输给了 uninformed\n    baselines。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7: Reward signal comparison'\n    columns:\n    - reward_type\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - pareto_dominated\n    rows:\n    - - action-change (ours)\n      - 21.9%\n      - 88%\n      - Yes (by all others)\n    - - random trigger\n      - 23.4%\n      - 52%\n      - 'No'\n    - - confidence-based\n      - 25.0%\n      - 65%\n      - 'No'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Action-change reward 是 worst performer。Claim 2 ('action-change is effective\n    intrinsic reward') 被彻底 falsified。Paper 失去了 selective verification 的 technical\n    contribution。\n- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router, head-to-head 对比。\n  expected_results:\n    ares_success: 0.25\n    ares_verification_rate: 0.55\n    ares_cost_reduction: 0.38\n    biavr_success: 0.219\n    biavr_verification_rate: 0.88\n    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.12\n    ares_dominates_biavr: true\n  result_rationale: ARES 用 SFT 从 oracle decisions 学 router，不需要 RL reward signal quality。在\n    same base agent 上 ARES 能学到 55% verification rate 且保持 success（因为它直接学 'when did\n    verification change outcome' from data），而 B-IAVR 依赖 noisy RL reward 学不到 meaningful\n    policy。ARES 在 Pareto frontier 上 dominate B-IAVR。我们不仅没有 '≥10pp better cost reduction'，反而被\n    dominated。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Pareto frontier with ARES point clearly dominating B-IAVR point.'\n  analysis: SFT approach (ARES) 优于 RL approach (B-IAVR) 在这个 setting 下。原因：SFT 有 oracle\n    supervision（从 data 直接学 when to verify），不受 reward noise 影响。RL 需要 good reward signal\n    但我们没有。Paper 的 'RL > SFT for selective verification' implicit claim 被反驳。\n- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_success: 0.15\n    step_independent_success: 0.12\n    ratio: 1.25\n    episode_level_std: 0.06\n    step_independent_std: 0.08\n    difference_significant: false\n    p_value: 0.38\n  result_rationale: Worst 档下 scienceworld_episode_vs_step_ratio 在 [0.8, 1.5]。Ratio=1.25\n    意味着 episode-level 只是 marginally better（15% vs 12%，差异 3pp not significant p=0.38）。ScienceWorld\n    有更短的 episodes（~10-15 steps vs ALFWorld 30-50），所以 step-independent 的 information\n    loss 没那么严重——shorter episodes = fewer windows = less sign misattribution。这反驳了 'episode-level\n    universally superior' claim，支持 'advantage depends on episode length' 的 nuanced\n    view，但也意味着我们的 contribution 是 domain-specific 而非 general。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: ScienceWorld transfer'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - std\n    - avg_episode_length\n    rows:\n    - - episode-level\n      - 15.0%\n      - 6pp\n      - 12.3 steps\n    - - step-independent (h=5)\n      - 12.0%\n      - 8pp\n      - 12.3 steps\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Episode-level advantage 不 generalize to shorter-horizon tasks。ScienceWorld\n    的短 episode 使 step-independent 的缺陷不 manifest。Reviewer concern #5 (single environment)\n    被证实——our finding is ALFWorld-specific (long horizon)，不是 general principle。'\n- name: 7B model scaling verification\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: Qwen3-7B 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent。\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_7b_success: 0.35\n    step_independent_7b_success: 0.22\n    delta_pp: 13\n    relative_improvement: 1.59\n    step_independent_collapse: false\n    step_independent_7b_h5_success: 0.18\n  result_rationale: 7B 模型更强，step-independent 不完全崩溃（22% vs 1.7B 的 0%）。原因：更大模型有更好的 in-context\n    learning，即使 h=5 窗口也能从有限 context 推断 partial strategy。Episode-level 仍优（35% vs 22%）但\n    gap 缩小（13pp vs 1.7B 的 28pp）。这进一步削弱 'catastrophic failure' narrative——在 stronger\n    model 上 step-independent 只是 suboptimal 而非 catastrophic。Reviewer 会问 'at what model\n    size does the gap disappear entirely?'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 9: 7B scaling'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - 1.7B\n    - 7B\n    - gap_reduction\n    rows:\n    - - episode-level\n      - 28.1%\n      - 35%\n      - —\n    - - step-independent (h=5)\n      - 0%\n      - 22%\n      - 'Gap: 28pp→13pp'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Episode-level advantage diminishes with model scale。7B step-independent\n    不崩溃（22%），gap 缩小到 13pp。暗示 'catastrophic failure' 是 small model + long horizon 的特定\n    interaction，更大模型的 in-context learning 能部分补偿 credit assignment 缺陷。Paper 的 alarm\n    ('step-independent catastrophically fails!') 变成了 'step-independent is suboptimal\n    for small models on long tasks'——much weaker claim。\n- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: 按 ALFWorld task type 分解 success。\n  expected_results:\n    pick_success: 0.35\n    clean_success: 0.25\n    heat_success: 0.3\n    cool_success: 0.2\n    examine_success: 0.15\n    pick_two_success: 0.1\n    episode_length_correlation: 0.45\n    longest_task_success: 0.1\n    shortest_task_success: 0.35\n  result_rationale: '较短 task（pick: ~15 steps）success 较高（35%），较长 task（pick_two: ~45\n    steps, examine: ~40 steps）success 最低（10-15%）。Episode length correlation=0.45 (moderate)。这\n    partially 支持 ''longer tasks benefit more from episode-level''，但 correlation 不够\n    strong——其他 factors（task complexity, number of required objects）也 matter。Not a\n    clean story。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Per-task breakdown'\n    columns:\n    - task_type\n    - success\n    - avg_episode_length\n    - step_indep_success\n    rows:\n    - - pick\n      - 35%\n      - '15'\n      - 8%\n    - - heat\n      - 30%\n      - '22'\n      - 3%\n    - - clean\n      - 25%\n      - '28'\n      - 0%\n    - - cool\n      - 20%\n      - '25'\n      - 2%\n    - - examine\n      - 15%\n      - '38'\n      - 0%\n    - - pick_two\n      - 10%\n      - '45'\n      - 0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: scatter plot success vs episode_length, with moderate negative trend (r=-0.45).'\n  analysis: Task length 是 contributing factor 但非唯一因素。Paper 可以 claim 'longer tasks\n    benefit more' 但不能 claim 'length is the mechanism'。Adds nuance but not a strong\n    independent contribution。\n","numLines":665,"startLine":1,"totalLines":665}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RiDycbJWgNpysqs3gPYG2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the PDF and the review context. Let me summarize what I know:\n\n**Paper**: \"Credit Assignment Granularity in Multi-Turn Agent RL: An Empirical Taxonomy of Failure Modes\"\n\nThe paper studies credit assignment granularity in multi-turn agent RL (ALFWorld), comparing step-independent GRPO, episode-level GRPO, and GAE. Key findings:\n1. Step-independent training has a stochastic performance cliff (seed-dependent)\n2. Episode-level GRPO plateaus at ~24%, far below GAE (44%)\n3. Selective verification (B-IAVR) fails completely - Pareto-dominated by naive baselines\n\n\n4. The original claim that coarser granularity is sufficient completely falls apart—GAE's fine-grained approach dominates, and the selective verification method contributes nothing of value\n\nNow I need to set up the review process with two parallel reviewers: one focusing on methods and experiments, another on novelty and related work. I'll then run them through a structured roundtable discussion where they independently evaluate, share findings, converge on key issues, and synthesize a final assessment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32481,"cache_read_input_tokens":24216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32481},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbfaf1eb-86b3-4c62-a538-5d4d55066586","uuid":"b84c0e57-3e16-4731-b64c-be646f30fd91"}
